From f75978ea3ae9f8e29152d98951604dd5070e208b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:02:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] parse: a statement-position `if`/`while` condition may call
 or index

kamadak-exif 0.6.1 src/tag.rs:1052 (fselect 0.10.3):

    match *value {
        Value::Rational(ref v) if v.len() > 0 =>
            if v[0].denom != 0xffffffff { .. } else { .. },

    error: Unexpected token TOK_SQUARE_OPEN, expected TOK_BRACE_OPEN

Parse_Stmt, which also parses match arm bodies, sets
`disallow_call_or_index` for a block-like expression (`if`, `while`,
`for`, `loop`, `match`), so `if c {} [1]` is a statement followed by
an array, not an index. `match` and `for` clear the flag for their own
operands, but the `if`/`while` conditions (Parse_IfLetChain) kept it, so
`v[0]` stopped after `v`. A function body's tail `if` didn't hit this;
only statement-position ones (arm bodies, block statements) did.

Parse_IfLetChain clears the flag for the conditions it parses. The
saved parse state restores it on return, for the token after the
block.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/parse/expr.cpp b/src/parse/expr.cpp
index da093b57..780af543 100644
--- a/src/parse/expr.cpp
+++ b/src/parse/expr.cpp
@@ -479,6 +479,11 @@ ExprNodeP Parse_ExprBlockLine_Stmt(TokenStream& lex, bool& has_semicolon)
 
 std::vector<AST::IfLet_Condition> Parse_IfLetChain(TokenStream& lex)
 {
+    // A fresh expression: `Parse_Stmt` disallows a call/index after a statement-like `if`/`while` (`if c {} [0]`), but
+    // that flag is for the token after the block, not for the condition (restored on return)
+    // - kamadak-exif 0.6.1 tag.rs:1052: `Value::Rational(ref v) if v.len() > 0 => if v[0].denom != 0xffffffff { .. }`
+    //   -> "Unexpected token TOK_SQUARE_OPEN, expected TOK_BRACE_OPEN"
+    CLEAR_PARSE_FLAG(lex, disallow_call_or_index);
     Token   tok;
     std::vector<AST::IfLet_Condition>   conditions;
     bool had_pat = false;
